# What git ignores. This must agree with the Local list in RepoFiles.txt,
# which is the readable statement of what lives here without being tracked.
# If the two ever disagree, RepoFiles.txt is the one the audit and cleanFileDir
# read, so fix this file to match it.

# Built by BuildFileDir. All of it can be rebuilt from the sources.
FileDir.exe
FileDir.dll
FileDirScript.dll
FileDir_setup.exe

# Generated by BuildFileDir, from version.txt and Hotkeys.ini. Do not edit
# these, and do not commit them: the build overwrites them every time.
Version.cs
KeyMap.cs

# Logs. Each script writes a fresh one beside itself on every run.
BuildFileDir.log
auditFileDir.log
cleanFileDir.log
makeKeyMap.log
tagRelease.log
postPage.log

# Taken from the EdSharp project at build time, not ours to redistribute.
Ude.dll

# Swept aside by cleanFileDir: kept on disk, never part of the project,
# and gone through by hand when there is time.
notes/

# The user's own quick links.
Quick/

# Left behind by a test installation.
unins000.dat
unins000.exe

# Media tools copied in from HomerScribe: well over 100 MB of third-party
# binaries, which do not belong in a git repository. The same list appears
# under Local in RepoFiles.txt, which is the one the scripts read.
System.Memory.dll
System.Buffers.dll
System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe.dll
exiftool.exe
ffmpeg.exe
ffprobe.exe
yt-dlp.exe

# Scratch files for capturing console output.
temp.txt
tmp.txt

# Working documents kept at the root but not part of FileDir. The same list
# appears under Local in RepoFiles.txt, which is the one the scripts read.
CamelType_Conversion_Notes.md
FileDir_Modernization_Transition_Brief.md
Handover.md

# Python's compiled cache, recreated whenever a script runs.
__pycache__/

# Editor and operating system noise.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.bak
*.tmp
*~
